<title>CHINA: Seapower Int'l yr net loss HK$55.51 mln.</title>
<headline>Seapower Int'l yr net loss HK$55.51 mln.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   10.9 loss  vs 8.4 gain</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    nil	  vs nil</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  44.39 loss vs 63.47 gain</p>
<p>    Net			    55.51 loss vs 40.00 profit</p>
<p>    Turnover		     414.09     vs 375.37 (see note)</p>
<p>    Company name		 Seapower International Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  September 19-25</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   N/A</p>
<p>NOTE - Seapower International Holdings engages in property investment and development and securities broking.</p>
<p>The comparative turnover has been changed from that previously reported HK$378.27 million to HK$375.37 million following the comments from the auditors.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional loss of HK$21.85 million on write off of fixed assets on Paramount group's factory removal, loss of HK$17.90 million on disposal of other land and buildings of the Paramount group, loss of HK$7.58 million deficit arising on revaluation of other land and buildings of the Paramount group and gain of 2.93 million on disposal of long term investments.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is nil vs nil.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
